{
  "id": "03-make-room-to-listen",
  "title": "Make Room to Listen",
  "tenet": "Walk with the Holy Spirit",
  "durationMs": 68265,
  "text": "Imagine a girl building a small stool with her grandfather. Eager to impress him, she measures, cuts, and hammers without stopping. When she stands the stool upright, it rocks. She pushes one corner down; another rises. Her grandfather kneels beside her and lays the pieces on the floor. \"Let's look at the legs together.\" This time she watches, asks questions, and listens before she cuts. She still does the work. But now she is learning as she works.\n\nWe can bring that willingness to our life with the Holy Spirit. Prayer is more than presenting a finished plan and asking God to approve it. Bring Him your work, your relationships, your uncertainty, and your decisions. Make room to listen through prayer and Scripture, with patience and wise counsel. You do not have to turn every thought into a message from God. Keep seeking Him, and remain willing to be corrected. Communion grows as we learn to walk with Him.\n\nBefore your next important decision, pause. Pray, listen, and consider what faithfulness asks of you. Make room for God before you rush ahead.",
